# core.autocrlf is on for this clone, which rewrites checked-out files to CRLF
# on Windows. Harmless for source, but these two are served to crawlers as
# literal bytes and are asserted on byte-for-byte by the test suite, so they
# must be identical on a developer's machine and on the Linux host.
public/sitemap.xml text eol=lf
public/robots.txt  text eol=lf
